From: David Lang <david@lang.hm>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: RNR: skip own BSS by BSSID, not by short SSID

SCALE local carry of the hostapd change that skips only this BSS's own
BSSID when building beacon RNR (IE 201), instead of every neighbor with
the same short SSID.

Stock hostapd_eid_nr_db() and hostapd_eid_nr_db_len() (src/ap/ieee802_11.c)
drop every nr_db entry whose short_ssid matches this AP, so same-ESS
neighbors never appear in the beacon Reduced Neighbor Report. Skip only
the entry whose BSSID equals hapd->own_addr.

Adds package/network/services/hostapd/patches/900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch
(verified at fuzz 0 on hostapd ca266cc2 plus OpenWrt 41a1874c's 63 hostapd
patches) and bumps PKG_RELEASE to 101.

Not submitted to the hostap mailing list yet. The upstream-form commit
is 391d276139c77c8648af6322458026c3fa0c7824 on local branch
rnr-allow-same-ssid-neighbors. There is no OpenWrt PR.

The deciding drop signal is the on-device behavioral test
(hostapd_rnr_same_ssid_test.sh) passing on an image built without this
patch (SOURCE_PATCH_MODE=trial SKIP_SOURCE_PATCHES=003), not the
presence of any upstream commit.

The scale-network branch wifi-kvr-mapper-ssid (959a419) assumes this fix.

---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile     |  2 +-
 .../900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch   | 40 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/services/hostapd/patches/900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index 3e14929..69eb4ec 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=101
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e3ff09c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/patches/900-scale-rnr-same-ssid-neighbors.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+From: David Lang <david@lang.hm>
+Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: RNR: skip own BSS by BSSID, not by short SSID
+
+hostapd_eid_nr_db_len() and hostapd_eid_nr_db() skip every neighbor
+database entry whose short SSID matches the reporting BSS, meaning to
+skip only the BSS's own entry (added by hostapd_neighbor_set_own_report).
+That also drops every same-ESS neighbor AP from the Reduced Neighbor
+Report (beacon IE 201), which are the entries that matter for roaming.
+Skip only the entry whose BSSID equals hapd->own_addr.
+
+SCaLE local patch; upstream submission to hostap pending.
+
+--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
++++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+@@ -7924,7 +7924,11 @@
+ 		if (!nr->nr || wpabuf_len(nr->nr) < 12)
+ 			continue;
+ 
+-		if (nr->short_ssid == hapd->conf->ssid.short_ssid)
++		/* Skip this BSS's own nr_db entry (hostapd_neighbor_set_own_report).
++		 * Match by BSSID, not short_ssid: same-ESS remote APs must remain
++		 * eligible for RNR; only avoid advertising ourselves. Other colocated
++		 * BSS BSSIDs stay eligible. */
++		if (ether_addr_equal(nr->bssid, hapd->own_addr))
+ 			continue;
+ 
+ 		/* Start a new element */
+@@ -8281,7 +8285,11 @@
+ 		if (!nr->nr || wpabuf_len(nr->nr) < 12)
+ 			continue;
+ 
+-		if (nr->short_ssid == hapd->conf->ssid.short_ssid)
++		/* Skip this BSS's own nr_db entry (hostapd_neighbor_set_own_report).
++		 * Match by BSSID, not short_ssid: same-ESS remote APs must remain
++		 * eligible for RNR; only avoid advertising ourselves. Other colocated
++		 * BSS BSSIDs stay eligible. */
++		if (ether_addr_equal(nr->bssid, hapd->own_addr))
+ 			continue;
+ 
+ 		/* Start a new element */
